rem graph.pnx - basic bench `graph`: breadth-first search from node 0 over a sparse graph (8 neighbours per node,
rem ((u * 2654435761) + k * 40503 + 1) mod n), the queue an array. pnx graph.pnx N (default 200000, up to 400000).
use io .
use env .
use str .
const most 400000
array adj int 3200000
array dist int most
array que int most
def main or fail do
  1 env.arg or_else to e "200000" end str.to_int or_fail to n
  0 n range do to u
    0 8 range do to k
      u 2654435761 mul  k 40503 mul add 1 add n mod  u 8 mul k add set adj
    end each
  end each
  0 n range do to i -1 i set dist end each
  0 0 set dist
  0 0 set que
  0 to qh
  1 to qt
  1 to seen
  loop
    qh qt lt not if break . end
    qh que idx to u
    qh 1 add to qh
    u dist idx to du
    0 8 range do to k
      u 8 mul k add adj idx to v
      v dist idx -1 eq if
        du 1 add v set dist
        qt n lt if v qt set que  qt 1 add to qt  seen 1 add to seen end
      end
    end each
  end
  0 to total
  0 n range do to i i dist idx to d  d 0 ge if total d add to total end end each
  args "graph " n " " seen " " total . cat io.println
end
main or_else to e args "graph: " e err_text . cat io.println end
